To set up this application professionally using **Vite** and **Tailwind CSS v4** (without the CDN), follow these steps.

Tailwind v4 changes the configuration workflow significantly by moving configuration from a JavaScript file (`tailwind.config.js`) directly into your CSS file using the `@theme` directive.

### Phase 1: Project Initialization & Installation

1.  **Scaffold the project** (if you haven't already):
    ```bash
    npm create vite@latest kriyadocs-rvs -- --template react-ts
    cd kriyadocs-rvs
    ```

2.  **Install Dependencies**:
    You need the React dependencies, the specific icons used in the code, and the new Tailwind v4 packages.
    ```bash
    npm install react react-dom lucide-react
    npm install tailwindcss @tailwindcss/vite
    ```

### Phase 2: Configuration Files

Here is the exact code you need to replace/create in your files to migrate your specific branding, colors, and animations from the CDN config to a build-time config.

#### 1. Update `vite.config.ts`
Tailwind v4 uses a Vite plugin instead of PostCSS configuration.

```typescript
import { defineConfig } from 'vite'
import react from '@vitejs/plugin-react'
import tailwindcss from '@tailwindcss/vite'
import path from 'path'

// https://vitejs.dev/config/
export default defineConfig({
  plugins: [
    react(),
    tailwindcss(), // <--- Add this
  ],
  resolve: {
    alias: {
      '@': path.resolve(__dirname, './src'),
    },
  },
})
```

#### 2. Create `src/index.css`
This is the most important step. We are migrating the JSON config from your `index.html` into CSS variables using Tailwind v4 syntax.

```css
@import "tailwindcss";

@theme {
  /* 1. Define Fonts */
  --font-sans: 'Inter', system-ui, sans-serif;

  /* 2. Define Brand Colors */
  --color-brand-50: #f5f0fa;
  --color-brand-100: #ebe4f5;
  --color-brand-200: #d4c6ea;
  --color-brand-300: #b69fdc;
  --color-brand-400: #9678cb;
  --color-brand-500: #7854b8;
  --color-brand-600: #5f259f; /* Kriyadocs Primary */
  --color-brand-700: #511e8a;
  --color-brand-800: #451a74;
  --color-brand-900: #2d104c;

  --color-orcid: #A6CE39;

  /* 3. Define Animations */
  --animate-fade-in-up: fadeInUp 0.6s ease-out forwards;
  --animate-fade-in: fadeIn 0.3s ease-out forwards;
  --animate-blob: blob 7s infinite;

  /* 4. Define Keyframes */
  @keyframes fadeInUp {
    0% { opacity: 0; transform: translateY(20px); }
    100% { opacity: 1; transform: translateY(0); }
  }

  @keyframes fadeIn {
    0% { opacity: 0; }
    100% { opacity: 1; }
  }

  @keyframes blob {
    0% { transform: translate(0px, 0px) scale(1); }
    33% { transform: translate(30px, -50px) scale(1.1); }
    66% { transform: translate(-20px, 20px) scale(0.9); }
    100% { transform: translate(0px, 0px) scale(1); }
  }
}

/* 5. Global Styles & Reset (Migrated from your index.html <style> block) */
:root {
  scroll-behavior: smooth;
  scrollbar-gutter: stable;
  scroll-padding-top: 5rem;
}

body {
  @apply bg-white antialiased text-slate-800;
  -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
  -moz-osx-font-smoothing: grayscale;
}

/* Modern Typography Enhancements */
h1, h2, h3, h4, h5, h6 {
  text-wrap: balance;
}

p {
  text-wrap: pretty;
}

/* Custom Scrollbar */
::-webkit-scrollbar {
  width: 8px;
  height: 8px;
}
::-webkit-scrollbar-track {
  background: transparent;
}
::-webkit-scrollbar-thumb {
  background: #d4c6ea;
  border-radius: 4px;
}
::-webkit-scrollbar-thumb:hover {
  background: #b69fdc;
}

/* Chrome Autofill Fix */
input:-webkit-autofill,
input:-webkit-autofill:hover, 
input:-webkit-autofill:focus, 
input:-webkit-autofill:active {
  -webkit-text-fill-color: #111827;
  transition: background-color 5000s ease-in-out 0s;
}
```

#### 3. Clean up `index.html`
Remove the Tailwind CDN script and the inline styles.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <title>Login | Kriyadocs RVS</title>

    <!-- Fonts -->
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
    <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Inter:wght@300;400;500;600;700;800&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
  </head>
  <body>
    <div id="root"></div>
    <!-- Vite handles the script injection -->
    <script type="module" src="/src/index.tsx"></script>
  </body>
</html>
```

#### 4. Update `src/index.tsx`
Ensure you import the CSS file created in Step 2.

```tsx
import React from 'react';
import ReactDOM from 'react-dom/client';
import App from './App';
import './index.css'; // <--- Import the new CSS file here

const rootElement = document.getElementById('root');
if (!rootElement) {
  throw new Error("Could not find root element to mount to");
}

const root = ReactDOM.createRoot(rootElement);
root.render(
  <React.StrictMode>
    <App />
  </React.StrictMode>
);
```

### Phase 3: Run the Application

1.  **Development:**
    ```bash
    npm run dev
    ```
    This will start the Vite server. Tailwind v4 is extremely fast and compiles your CSS on demand.

2.  **Production Build:**
    ```bash
    npm run build
    ```
    This will generate a `dist` folder with optimized assets, including a tiny, purged CSS file containing only the styles you actually used.

### Why this approach is better:
1.  **Performance:** No runtime calculation of CSS classes (which the CDN does).
2.  **Bundle Size:** The final CSS file will be very small.
3.  **Intellisense:** If you use VS Code, install the "Tailwind CSS IntelliSense" extension. With this setup, you will get autocomplete for your custom classes like `bg-brand-600` or `animate-fade-in`.
4.  **Modern:** Tailwind v4 uses native CSS variables, making the browser dev tools much easier to read and debug.

